{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And on the seventh day, seven bulls.</b> The bulls of the seven days of the festival total seventy, corresponding to the fifty-two Sabbaths and the seven days of Passover and the one day of Atzeret and the one day of Rosh HaShanah and the one day of Yom HaKippurim and the eight days of the festival in the year — they total seventy. Rashi explained that they correspond to seventy nations, and in the days of the Temple they protect them from suffering; therefore Scripture punished them in the book of Zechariah for the festival of Sukkot more than for other commandments, because the bull-offerings of the festival of Sukkot protect them."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:11.646092227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}